 </div>
 <div>
 <h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:2rem">Mistakes Relocators Make</h2>
 <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column">
-<details class="accordion-item"><summary class="accordion-q">Buying in the wrong neighborhood for their lifestyle</summary><div class="accordion-a"><p>The Grand Strand is not one market. A family relocating from the suburbs of Charlotte who buys an oceanfront condo in Myrtle Beach city often finds the area too touristy and lacking the suburban feel they expected. Spend time in multiple neighborhoods on your visit before narrowing down. We build a neighborhood tour into every relocation plan.</p></div></details>
-<details class="accordion-item"><summary class="accordion-q">Underestimating coastal insurance costs</summary><div class="accordion-a"><p>Buyers from inland markets are accustomed to one homeowners insurance policy. In coastal SC you need three: homeowners, wind/hail, and flood. Together these can add $400 to $700 per month to your housing cost. Get insurance quotes during your due diligence period, not after.</p></div></details>
-<details class="accordion-item"><summary class="accordion-q">Not getting pre-approved before shopping</summary><div class="accordion-a"><p>Out-of-state buyers sometimes start touring before completing their pre-approval, assuming they can transfer a pre-approval letter from their current state. SC lenders underwrite coastal properties differently, particularly for condos, flood-zone properties, and investment purchases. Get your pre-approval with a SC-licensed lender before you tour. Our preferred lender, BrickWood Mortgage, is SC-licensed and can pre-approve you directly.</p></div></details>
-<details class="accordion-item"><summary class="accordion-q">Relying on Zillow neighborhood data instead of local knowledge</summary><div class="accordion-a"><p>Zillow's neighborhood ratings do not reflect the block-by-block differences in the Grand Strand market. A zip code that looks average in the statistics may contain a top-rated school district, a golf-cart-friendly community, or a high-performing STR corridor. Ask your agent for a block-by-block breakdown before drawing conclusions from online ratings.</p></div></details>
